  "status": "declared_local_transition_contract",
  "scope": "Pure ConversationFloor control semantics. Prefixes are typed control signals; they do not open devices or establish acoustic playback, capture, recognition, or stale worker/turn correlation.",
  "oracle": "Independently declared expected outcomes, never imported or generated from the production private transition table. Every context/event cell is explicit; null requires InvalidConversationTransition and an unchanged snapshot.",
  "revision_semantics": "Increment once only when state or candidate_return_state changes. Legal no-ops return the identical immutable snapshot; rejected signals preserve that object and revision.",
  "candidate_semantics": "A candidate retains its current underlying response floor across playback changes and response completion. Rejection restores that latest floor. Playback may not restart after the candidate's response has finished.",
